#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PHASE 9 - PAGE 43: CLOSING - INTRO
// Shadow Work Philosopher: 200+ words on individuation and identity integration
// Mirroring technique included

#somatic_page(
  title: "Phase 9: Closing – The New Identity",
  body_text: [
    #align(center)[
      _"No tree, it is said, can grow to heaven unless its roots reach down to hell."_
      
      — C.G. Jung
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    You may feel a strange mixture of emotions as you arrive at this final phase—perhaps grief for the self you are leaving behind, or a quiet pride beginning to swell in your chest. Your body may feel different than it did when you opened this journal. Lighter in some places. More rooted in others. *You are not the same person who began this work. Take a moment to honor what you have become.*
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #rect(fill: rgb("#F5F5F0"), stroke: 0.5pt + gray, inset: 15pt, radius: 2pt)[
      Jung called it *individuation*: the lifelong process of becoming who you truly are by integrating all parts of the psyche—light and shadow, masculine and feminine, persona and authentic self. You have done this sacred work. You have descended into the depths, met the parts of yourself you had exiled, and brought them back into the wholeness of your being.
      
      Individuation is not about perfection—it is about *completeness*. The integrated person is not someone who has no darkness; they are someone who has *befriended* their darkness, transforming it from an unconscious saboteur into a conscious ally. They carry both their wounds and their gifts with dignity. They no longer project their shadow onto the world, because there is nothing left to disown.
      
      This final phase is about *consolidation*—gathering the threads of your transformation into a coherent new identity. An identity that includes your Inner Child, your fears, your rage, your brilliance. An identity that is no longer at war with itself. The work does not end here, of course. But you are different now. You have tools. You have awareness. You have proven to yourself that you can face what lives in the depths and return, transformed. This is the hero's journey, completed in your own psyche. Welcome home.
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    *In this phase, you will:*
    - Reflect deeply on how you have changed through this journey
    - Create an "Anti-Sabotage Shield" to protect your transformation
    - Write a new story for yourself—one that includes your wholeness
    - Perform a closing ritual to mark the transition into your new life
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
